From: Kernix <kernix@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: describe BCLK clock selection

The Kernix Pi Zero board uses simple-audio-card and has no MCLK wire.
Expose the existing BCLK PLL path through an opt-in device property.
The controller uses unpadded stereo frames and continuous clocks.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Kernix <kernix@localhost>
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tlv320dac3100.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tlv320dac3100.yaml
@@ -56,6 +56,13 @@
   IOVDD-supply: true
 
   DVDD-supply: true
+
+  ti,pll-bclk:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      Use incoming BCLK as the PLL reference instead of MCLK. The serial
+      audio controller must supply BCLK with no padding bits between samples
+      and must keep the clock running while the codec is active.
 
   reset-gpios:
     description: GPIO specification for the active low RESET input.
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/simple-card.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/simple-card.yaml
@@ -190,6 +190,10 @@
     $ref: "#/definitions/frame-inversion"
   simple-audio-card,bitclock-inversion:
     $ref: "#/definitions/bitclock-inversion"
+  simple-audio-card,continuous-clock:
+    description: Keep the serial clock running while the audio link is active.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
+
   simple-audio-card,format:
     $ref: "#/definitions/format"
   simple-audio-card,mclk-fs:
